Z||000014||Indiana_resto_guy||09-21-2001||08:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>I thought it was very impressive.<P>And I did get the feeling too that Hillary was sometimes less than enthousiastic.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B>I liked it.<BR>There was a moment when Hillary's clapping didn't look very enthusiastic.  Hmmm...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I am sure that Hillary thought that the wimp she still has ties to (not too tight I would imagine), That never in his life could Bill make a speech like that let alone make a decision of this magnitude.<BR>I am certain the he would be hiding under a desk or something right now wondering where to get his next blow job!<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B>yeah he made a point, but between pauses he is trying so hard not smirk cuz he is thinking, they actually clapping for me, they like me. he think he Mr. Cool and great being president. I like Clinton so much better than him. I just wonder what Gore would have did. Bush is such loser.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Everyone has an opinion Kyle, and your entitled to yours! Myself, I was clapping for the man, for the decision and for the words! Billy Boy could never had rallied the senate in this fashion. We have all witnessed his techniques in action or rather lack of it. The Gore issue has already been handled! In time I am sure that you will see that President Bush will turn out to be a winner! I think that he is doing the right things and his really doing his homework!<BR>How about you?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||stimpy||09-21-2001||08:38 AM||||I don't like Bush. I'll get that out of the way right now. I think he looks like a chimp and has the IQ of a bottlecap. He is a very uncharismatic speaker, and like Kyle, uses horrible grammer.<P>That being said, I am glad he won the coin toss that we call the election process that put him in office. I think he is gullible and easily led enough to listen and approve the decisions of his advisors and cabinet.  Personally, I think that Colin Powell is doing a fine job to rid the world of "tera" and "tereris"<P>I tink Hillary was bored because she is a HELLUVA better public speaker then Curious George. But it was tacky. She should have realized the cameras would hit her.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fformula88||09-21-2001||09:11 AM||||First off I am not a big supporter of bush, nor did I vote for him in the election.<P>However, I do feel he has handled the situation well so far.  Time will tell if he is truly the right man for the job.  He did a VERY good job with his speech, considering he isn't the greatest speaker!<P>I think Bush is really a smart guy, but his smallish vocabulary and less than impressive public speaking skills lead me to believe he isn't all that well read.  That doesn't mean he cannot handle this job at all.  He seems to be able to reason everything well, and in Chaney and Powell he has to incredibly intelligent advisors, both experienced in the Iraq conflict.<P>Can anyone imagine Gore's version of the speech last night?  "We will take the terrorists... and put them in a 'Lock Box'"!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  hehe||||reg||1
Z||000017||87ECO5||09-21-2001||09:35 AM||||Hillary needed to check her attitude at the door.  Bush should have mentioned Canada in our list of true friends.<P>Other than those, great speach!  I'm fired up ...||||reg||6
Z||000018||Formula88||09-21-2001||09:57 AM||||I agree Canada should have been mentioned.  And for those who don't like Bush, think about this...   You not only have Bush, but you have his Cabinet.  You can't argue that Bush's Cabinet has the right people in the right places to help any President deal with this situation.  Gore's Cabinet wouldn't be nearly as well staffed for this type of crisis.<P>Also, I think Bush wasn't smirking so much because he thinks they like him, but because he's moved by the solidarity of the U.S. people and the Congress.  How often does that happen?  Hell, I was smiling watching it on T.V.<P>May God Bless America and the World in the coming fight.||||reg||6
Z||000019||frontal lobe||09-21-2001||10:49 AM||||Stimpy, which Hillary are you talking about being a good speaker???  The compationless, nasal, whiny, yes-I-am-a-woman-but-I-am-more-of-a-man-than-any-of-you self-serving condescending I-know-better-than-you-so-just-do-what-I-tell-you dead fish hag that is currently a senator?<P>Next statement not directed at you Stimpy but in general:  the people with the highest IQ's and the best speakers aren't necessarily the best leaders.  That's why there was never an Einstein/Dale Carnegie ticket in history.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Black88GT||09-21-2001||11:30 AM||||Stimpy, all I hear from people still upset about the election is how "dumb" Bush is.  Do dumb people go to Yale and Harvard?  I would hope not considering the requirements/reputation.<P><BR>I loved the speech.  Thought it was great.  I never liked Hillary Rodham Carpetbagger, and I would laugh if Guiliani changed his mind about running for the Senators position in a couple years, he would win by a land slide.<P>||||reg||12
Z||000021||Voytek||09-21-2001||11:59 AM||||Frontal lobe - bravo!  I couldn't have said it better myself.  Even though I'm a Canadian I have followed US politics fairly close.<P>Many times a good speaker is the one that is a good actor, i.e. Gore, and it is the honest speaker that places more value on the content than on the delivery.<P>I also don't believe public speaking is a good measure of a person's IQ.  The day you obtain official results of Mr. Bush's IQ Stimpy, be sure to post them on here.  Otherwise try to stick to facts.<P>He listens to his advisors?  NO, you're kidding me!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  My last definition of an advisor was one who provides advice or direction.<P>As far as Mr. Bush looking like a chimp - I think this is inappropriate at this time, but at least he doesn't look like a Big Mac or play with cigars.<P>Oh, and I'm not offended that he didn't mention Canada - we are an obvious partner.  On the other hand, I don't know if I would want to work with our prime minister either.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
