Z||000032||Dslice||09-21-2001||10:28 PM||||It was ok, but it wasnt great. I think he said the right things but he's not the most dynamic speaker he's no Ronald Reagan.I almost feel asleep. He got the Job done though. I thought the new cabinet position was a good Idea.||||reg||1
Z||000033||Fiero5||09-21-2001||11:04 PM||||How quickly they forget.<BR>Bush didn't win the majority vote. Gore lost the "electoral" vote. There is a difference. Gore won the popular (majority) vote. Does anyone know what that really means? It means that if Presidents were voted in like any other vote we have on things, Gore would be President. But we do this electoral thing that worked OK in the early years, but is pretty outdated now.<P>I agree that Bush is a bonehead who couldn't come up with a good speach or think on his feet if his life depended on it. And he doesn't have to, he has writers and spin people to do that for him. As was mentioned earlier, he does smirk alot. He looks like a little kid in 3rd grade who was just picked by the teacher to be the crossing guard in the playground for the day.<P>Yes his speach was great. Yes it had all the words we wanted to hear. "His" writers and cabinet members did a good job in getting it worded just right. His delivery was good, but not great. There were times when he should have been a bit angry in some parts during his delivery of it to show that we as a nation are not going to be F**cked with. They were saying after the speach was over, how his speach had certain phrases that can be quoted as memorable phrases for years down the road. The phrases and wording got the applause. I am sure if General Stormin Normin gave that same speach, he would have gotten the same response.<BR>It was really the speach that touched us. I will admit that it must have been pretty impressive to many accross the world to hear THE President of the United States saying what he said. How would you have liked being a fly on the wall in the room where $hithead Bin Laden was sitting watching that speach?<P>It's true that it is still way to early to say whether or not 'ole George dubya will be a great president. We can wonder that all day long, but only time will tell.<BR>The bottom line is that George W. Bush is our president, and we have to stay united not only now because of this horrible tragedy, but for all time - good and bad. <BR>Let's not take our anger out on the innocent, especially on those innocent people who simply may look or sound like those we believe caused all this horror.<BR>We need to stay focused and make sure ALL Americans, and those we can call friends in other countries all over the world, are treated equally. Yes, this was an attack on Americans. But in the big picture, it was also an attack on humanity.<P>May God bless us<P>Steve<BR><P>------------------<BR>                                <IMG SRC="http://a1040.g.akamai.net/f/1040/759/1h/206.29.192.139/info/pics/sept11.jpg">                             <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||7
Z||000034||Patrick's Dad||09-22-2001||09:59 PM||||Oh boy, here we go again....<P>F5, Algore lost 34 states, including his own. How's that for a majority? And the fact is, GW only did enough to ensure his victory (conservation of energy & funds. Pretty smart in my book). If it were a simple majority vote (A democracy, which is a form of government we don't live in....), then he could have just stumped more in Texas, his own state, and won by a landslide.||||reg||5
Z||000035||FieroKyle||09-23-2001||10:08 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B> He is a very uncharismatic speaker, and like Kyle, uses horrible grammer.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, I didn't go edit my statement thousands of times to get it perfect, but I should since every one here picks apart everyone's statements untill they favor theirs or are politcally correct. Guess I should have wrote two drafts and had it proofread by my English 11 teacher, then okayed it with my lawyer before I posted on this forum. I'll remember this for next time.<P>Anyways, I knew people would *****  at me for it because everyone has their own opinions. I am alright with it. I am not mad at anyone even stimpy, (I usually agree with Stimpy more times than not and is pretty funny on the forum) just giving a update back to my earlier statement. I just can't get over two things, him being a coke head trying to become a stiff, and two, he was trying so hard not smirk between pauses in his address to the nation. I still think he thinks he is all hot ****  because is president. I still think he is weasle and wonder why people support him. Not saying McCain and Gore were much better, but Gore still in my mind is compared to Bush. But I have my reasons for things and you guys have yours.<P>Now re-reading my above statements, I see I put "I still think he" in the beginning of two sentences in a row. So what, pick it apart all you want and call me a grammar dumbass. Go ahead, make my day.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000036||FieroKyle||09-23-2001||10:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>I don't like Bush. I'll get that out of the way right now. I think he looks like a chimp and has the IQ of a bottlecap. He is a very uncharismatic speaker, and like Kyle, uses horrible grammer.<P>That being said, I am glad he won the coin toss that we call the election process that put him in office. I think he is gullible and easily led enough to listen and approve the decisions of his advisors and cabinet.  Personally, I think that Colin Powell is doing a fine job to rid the world of "tera" and "tereris"<P>I tink Hillary was bored because she is a HELLUVA better public speaker then Curious George. But it was tacky. She should have realized the cameras would hit her.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree with ya there further reading this and not just stopping at the point of comparing me to President Bush.<P>Two, Clinton was a fun president at least, and thought he did a great job as president. As far cheating on Hillary, thats his business and I not gonna hold his personal affairs on his abbillity to run the country. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000037||LZeitgeist||09-24-2001||01:57 PM||||Yeah, *that*'s what we need in office right now, a FUN President!!! Whoohoo!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>(Oh, and that whole 'lying under oath' thing must have just been a harmless prank! Wow, what a kidder!! I think I'll lie under oath the next time I'm in court and see how it works for me! Whoohoo!!)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000038||LarryB||09-24-2001||02:24 PM||||Based pm your logic, it would have been OK if it turned out Clinton had molested his daughter as well. After all, that would be his personal business!!!<P>The president is expected to set a good and positive example for the rest of the country.  In that, and in many other areas, Clinton was a total failure as president, and IMO he was one of the 3 worst presidents in the last 65 years.  (So was Carter, but he was a good man, just a bad president.)<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B> . As far cheating on Hillary, thats his business and I not gonna hold his personal affairs on his abbillity to run the country. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000039||FieroKyle||09-24-2001||03:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LarryB:<BR><B>Based pm your logic, it would have been OK if it turned out Clinton had molested his daughter as well. After all, that would be his personal business!!!<P>The president is expected to set a good and positive example for the rest of the country.  In that, and in many other areas, Clinton was a total failure as president, and IMO he was one of the 3 worst presidents in the last 65 years.  (So was Carter, but he was a good man, just a bad president.)<P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well cheating on a wife isn't a crime, just an issue of morals. I am not saying its right. Molesting is against the law. Your now talking about apples and oranges.<P>I would like to know how Clinton was a total failure, then also get relelected by a landslide. Now if anything, that doesn't make sense.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000040||Butter||09-24-2001||04:31 PM||||The speech, in my opinion, was the most powerful, most demanding and most unified presidential speech I have every heard or read of in the history of this country.  It has sent a clear message to the terrorist world.  This country along with most of the rest of the world appears to stand behind the message.  None of the decent folks I have ever been around wants to loose the progress their country has made.  I have been almost half way around the world and returned to the place where I understand the values of my area best but I know it is not the only way to live or enjoy life.<P>I respect the values of other people that promote life especially in varied ways.  The world as a whole has much to learn from these different ways of promoting life.  I am very much against the folks who think and push that their way of life is the only way.  Those people appear to use death as a way to unify their cause.  History has shown this to be true.<P>As far as who delivered the speech, well I’ve heard better speakers but the sentiment was well delivered.  The president is only as good as the cabinet he chooses and I think he has a good cabinet to draw from.  We all must be united in this effort to stop terrorism least we all will fall to a bunch of rag headed bearded freaks that are willing to hide behind a religion in order to rally the decent rag headed bearded folks to die for their one way cause.<P>I believe in this case the U.S. must all be Democans and Republicrats.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000041||LarryB||09-24-2001||05:26 PM||||In a number of states, adultery is still a prosecutorial crime.  In those states that retain fault grounds for divorce, it by itself is sufficient cause to grant the divorce when the innocent party has filed. Some states waive any waiting period to make the divorce final and/or alter the distribution of assets to favor the innocent party as well.  So, it's NOT apples and oranges.<P>It still stands that Clinton disgraced himself, but he also disgraced the office which he held and dishonored the people which he purported to serve.  <P>As far as why Clinton got reelected, P.T. Barnum put it best with "there's a sucker born every minute...". Except in this case there were a lot of suckers.<P>BTW, keep in mind that Bill Clinton wasn't elected with a majority of votes his first time around either; he got 43% of the popular vote. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B> Well cheating on a wife isn't a crime, just an issue of morals. I am not saying its right. Molesting is against the law. Your now talking about apples and oranges.<P>I would like to know how Clinton was a total failure, then also get relelected by a landslide. Now if anything, that doesn't make sense.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000042||mrfixit58||09-25-2001||07:48 PM||||I must say that, after reading all of the posts on this topic, I'm pleasantly pleased to see all the objectivity, even from those who did not vote for Bush. However, I can't help but comment on a few posts:<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>I don't like Bush. ... I think he looks like a chimp and has the IQ of a bottlecap. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's true your entitled to your opinion. I'm just glad we didn't elect all our Presidents based on how they looked. Besides most being old, fat, and out of shape, I believe one had wooden teeth (until his real dentures were made), one was a self educated lawyer with a ruddy completion, slumping posture and an ugly mole on his face, and another was a virtual paraplegic. Of course I'm speaking of Washington, Lincoln, and Roosevelt.<P>As to IQ, well. I think the President is judged best by the mark he leaves. This is MOSTLY a reflection of his and his cabinet's successes and the results of his polices. Time will tell.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>...all I hear from people still upset about the election is how "dumb" Bush is</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I believe Bush graduated from an Ivy League College, and Gore dropped out of one.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>He did a VERY good job with his speech, considering he isn't the greatest speaker</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree. I am equally sure that, somewhere in history, you'll probably find a President who had more than his share of speech problems. I remember Reagan stammering a few times myself. If anyone caught the musical tribute to American heros last Friday night, you also should have noticed some of Hollywoods biggest stars stammering through their tribute. Live performances are difficult to get perfect.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Bush didn't win the majority vote. Gore lost the "electoral" vote. There is a difference. Gore won the popular (majority) vote. Does anyone know what that really means?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, absolutely NOTHING! Except that either you failed Social Studies or you've obviously bought into the liberal media's line of crap. First off, the USA is a REPUBLIC (look it up in your Social Studies book and get back to us when you can argue your point). Second, Gore won only the popular votes that were counted. Remember, all the military votes for all the states were NOT counted and history and fact have proven that they are ALWAYS heavily Republican. The difference in the counted "popular" vote margin was so small, if if the military votes had been counted, Bush would also become the POPULAR President.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Since when does personal OPINION have to be supported by fact? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hummm... I'll have to remember that next time someone makes the statement about my Fiero being a fire trap.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Well cheating on a wife isn't a crime, just an issue of morals.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's true for the most part. Kinda like the link that was circulated a little while ago about outdated laws. It would be hard to convict someone of that these days. But, lieing under oath to the Grand Jury IS against the law. Remember, Clinton was impeached.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Clinton was a fun president at least, and thought he did a great job as president.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm still waiting on someone to give me a plausible example of Clinton being "fun" and what he did that was so "good". Someone please get back to me on that one.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>I would like to know how Clinton was a total failure, then also get relelected by a landslide. Now if anything, that doesn't make sense.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Your right. That truly is an oxymoron. My guess is his opponent was considered too old. Unfortunately, the American people place way too much importance on looks rather than character. It's truly sad.<P>Having said all that, I thought his speech was very moving. However, all the speeches and all the media rhetoric never moved me more that the image of the woman, with tear running down here cheek, passing out pictures of her missing husband to the fireman digging through the rubble.<P>God Bless America,<P><BR>------------------<BR>Roy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by mrfixit58 (edited 09-25-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000043||FieroKyle||09-25-2001||10:52 PM||||Clinton was impeached, but however not found guilty. When I mean by "fun", I mean he was always doing something controversal to his personal life and all the story to it, in which people like Jay Leno turn in it to something humorous. Like I said I don't agree with Clinton on him cheating. Also you say he didn't do anything good? I am still waiting for what he did bad? (other than the Lewinksy scandal). And all polls say that they had on headlines news had Clinton on the top 5 presidents ever list (he came in 5th of course). Just polls though, so don't flame on me about that information and exactness on it.||||reg||1
Z||000044||mrfixit58||09-26-2001||07:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B>. Also you say he didn't do anything good? I am still waiting for what he did bad? (other than the Lewinksy scandal). And all polls say that they had on headlines news had Clinton on the top 5 presidents ever list (he came in 5th of course). Just polls though, so don't flame on me about that information and exactness on it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>As if lying under oath, gays in the military (then gays out of the military), Lewinsky, and insider trading weren't enough? Just think... if all of our Presidents were so self serving what would our country be like? Or, would it even be here?<P>Yes, Clinton was President during one of the most prosperous times in American history but what did he do to make that happen? Nothing that I know of, except, leave alone the policies that Reagan put into place and Bush supported. Again, if someone knows different, I'm listening.<P>I'm not saying that George W. Bush will be the greatest President since George Washington. But his principles and convictions at least appear to be more of a servant of the people then of self. Only time will tell.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||1
